!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-namespace-type-leaving-its-key-family-unstated-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §7.2"
  description: """
    A namespace type is an instance of the kernel's `namespace`, and its keys are names of the family `key_type`
    states. `key_type` is a required field of `namespace`, and `hosted` leaves it out, so the construction is
    refused: no host supplies a namespace's key family. A record's fields are no namespace: `field_map` is an ordered
    map keyed by text, each key judged by the record's `name_type`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
